  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community based wild fire management in  Bombali District.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There is an alarming rate of bush fire in the Bombali District and this has had a negative impact on the environment and communities. Therefore, the need for an integrated approach to bush fire management is becoming increasingly apparent. The important function forests maintain in protecting communities from other forms of natural disaster such as wind storms and flooding is also a major issue related to bush fire
This project aims to pilot a community based approach in 3 communities in Sella Limba Chiefdom -Bombali District   to enable them actively participate in bush fire management planning.  It also integrates all activities related to fire management such as prevention, preparedness, suppression and restoration into one coordinated bush fire management approach. This initiative will also ensure that trees; especially economic trees are protected from wild fire destruction during the dry season so as to contribute towards environmental protection and sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
